1bi
The agent tumbles the block until it lands stably in a relatively similar orientation to the goal block. The agent is heavily punished for having the block be far from the palm (i.e. dropping the block) and having a high velocity, so it ends with the block in a stable position.
1bii
The agent is punished too harshly for exerting forces on the block, so its most highly rewarded option is to stay still.
1biii
The agent is only punished for exerting forces, and velocity, position, and orientation have no affect on the reward, so it learns to exert no forces and let the block fall freely.